RIGOROUS THEOREMS ON THE CAYLEY LINE
============================================================

THEOREM A: CAYLEY-DIRICHLET CONVOLUTION
----------------------------------------
If d*q = n, then (x_d + x_q)/(1 + x_d*x_q) = x_n.

Proof: LHS num = (d-1)(q+1)+(q-1)(d+1) = 2dq-2 = 2(n-1)
       LHS den = (d+1)(q+1)+(d-1)(q-1) = 2dq+2 = 2(n+1)
       LHS = (n-1)/(n+1) = x_n.  QED

  d=2,q=6,n=12: 11/13 = 11/13: True
  d=3,q=4,n=12: 11/13 = 11/13: True
  d=5,q=7,n=35: 17/18 = 17/18: True

THEOREM B: MULTIPLICATIVE = EXPONENTIAL
----------------------------------------
If f is completely multiplicative and continuous,
define F(t) = f(e^{2t}). Then F(t+s) = F(t)F(s).
Cauchy: F(t) = e^{ct}, so f(n) = n^{c/2}.  QED

THEOREM C: EULER TOTIENT
----------------------------------------
phi(n)/n = prod_{p|n} (1 - Q(x_p)^{-1})

Proof: (p-1)/p = 2x_p/(1+x_p) = 1 - 1/Q(x_p).  QED

  p=2: (p-1)/p=1/2, 1-1/Q(x_p)=1/2: True
  p=3: (p-1)/p=2/3, 1-1/Q(x_p)=2/3: True
  p=5: (p-1)/p=4/5, 1-1/Q(x_p)=4/5: True
  p=7: (p-1)/p=6/7, 1-1/Q(x_p)=6/7: True
  p=11: (p-1)/p=10/11, 1-1/Q(x_p)=10/11: True

THEOREM D: DELANNOY EXPANSION OF PRIME POWERS
----------------------------------------
For prime p, integer m >= 1:
  p^m = 1 + 2*sum_{k=1}^inf g_k(m)*((p-1)/(p+1))^k

Proof: Q(x)^m = 1 + 2*sum g_k(m)*x^k. Set x = x_p. QED

  p=2,m=1: sum=2.000000, p^m=2, err=1.46e-14
  p=2,m=2: sum=4.000000, p^m=4, err=8.89e-13
  p=2,m=3: sum=8.000000, p^m=8, err=2.71e-11
  p=3,m=1: sum=3.000000, p^m=3, err=3.73e-09
  p=3,m=2: sum=9.000000, p^m=9, err=2.31e-07
  p=3,m=3: sum=26.999993, p^m=27, err=7.18e-06
  p=5,m=1: sum=4.999969, p^m=5, err=3.13e-05
  p=5,m=2: sum=24.997997, p^m=25, err=2.00e-03
  p=5,m=3: sum=124.935510, p^m=125, err=6.45e-02

THEOREM E: EVEN g_k FROM FUNCTIONAL EQUATION
----------------------------------------
Q^m * Q(-x)^m = 1 implies:
  g_{2k} = sum_{j=1}^{2k-1} (-1)^{j+1} g_j g_{2k-j}

  m=5, g_2: actual=25, predicted=25, match=True
  m=5, g_4: actual=225, predicted=225, match=True
  m=5, g_6: actual=985, predicted=985, match=True
  m=7, g_2: actual=49, predicted=49, match=True
  m=7, g_4: actual=833, predicted=833, match=True
  m=7, g_6: actual=6321, predicted=6321, match=True

THEOREM F: 1/n^2 CANCELLATION
----------------------------------------
The functional equation at k=1: g_2(m) = g_1(m)^2 = m^2.

Expansion of CV^2:
  k=1 term: 2(n-2)/(n(n-1)) = 2/n - 2/n^2 + O(1/n^3)
  k=2 term: 2(n-4)^2/(n)_4 = 2/n^2 + O(1/n^3)
  Sum at 1/n^2: -2 + 2 = 0.  QED

The vanishing is FORCED by g_2 = g_1^2, which comes from
[x^2] log Q^m = 0 (the even log-coefficient vanishes).

THEOREM G: LOG STRUCTURE
----------------------------------------
log Q^m = 2m*arctanh(x) = 2m*(x + x^3/3 + x^5/5 + ...)
[x^k] log Q^m = 2m/k for odd k, 0 for even k.

Proof: log((1+x)/(1-x)) = log(1+x) - log(1-x)
  = (x-x^2/2+x^3/3-...) - (-x-x^2/2-x^3/3-...)
  = 2x + 2x^3/3 + 2x^5/5 + ... = 2*arctanh(x).  QED

THEOREM H: UNIQUENESS OF arctanh
----------------------------------------
arctanh is the unique odd FPS f with exp(f) rational of degree (1,1).

Proof: f odd, R=exp(f)=P/Q coprime. R(-x)=exp(-f)=1/R(x).
P(-x)Q(x) = P(x)Q(-x). Coprimality: P(-x)=cQ(x).
c=1 from f(0)=0. Degree (1,1): Q=1-ax, P=1+ax.
f = log((1+ax)/(1-ax)) = 2*arctanh(ax).  QED

THEOREM I: WICK ROTATION
----------------------------------------
arctanh(ix) = i*arctan(x). In particular arctanh(i) = i*pi/4.

Proof: arctanh(ix) = sum (ix)^{2k+1}/(2k+1)
  = i*sum (-1)^k x^{2k+1}/(2k+1) = i*arctan(x).  QED

============================================================
CATALOG OF PROVED RESULTS
============================================================

A. Hyp addition = Dirichlet divisor (algebraic identity)
B. Multiplicative = exponential (Cauchy functional equation)
C. phi(n)/n = prod(1-Q^{-1}) (algebraic identity)
D. p^m = 1+2*sum g_k*x_p^k (master GF at prime address)
E. g_{2k} from g_{odd} (functional equation Q*Q(-x)=1)
F. 1/n^2 cancels (consequence of g_2=g_1^2 from log structure)
G. Log-coefficients: 2m/k odd, 0 even (arctanh expansion)
H. arctanh unique odd FPS with rational exp (coprimality)
I. Wick rotation: arctanh(i)=i*pi/4 (series substitution)
